      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Craig Casey picked ahead of Jamison Gibson-Park for Argentina Test start",
          "body": "Craig Casey was handed the start over Jamison Gibson-Park in midweek and, in RTÉ's player ratings, earned an 8.5 for his display in Friday's 42-12 win over Argentina. Partnered with Sam Prendergast, who scored a solo try and kicked all six conversions, the pair controlled a Test game for the first time together, according to former Ireland scrum-half Conor Murray on the Ireland Rugby Social podcast. Murray added that Prendergast will now have a target on his back."
        },
