          "kicker": "Turin defeat",
          "heading": "Azzurri concede nine tries in 66-7 defeat to Springboks in Turin",
          "body": "Injury-hit Italy were overrun at the Allianz Stadium, where South Africa ran in nine tries, Sacha Feinberg-Mngomezulu contributing a solo try and 21 points, and led 45-0 at half-time. Italy were missing a 16-strong list of unavailable players, including captain Michele Lamaro and centres Tommaso Menoncello and Juan Ignacio Brex, and this was their fourth straight defeat. South Africa, who sit top of the Southern Hemisphere standings on 20 points, next face France in Paris."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
