          "kicker": "Missed chances",
          "heading": "Eddie Jones says Japan missed chances as Wales held on 28-21",
          "body": "Japan coach Eddie Jones said the 28-21 defeat in Cardiff was one that got away: \"That could have been a historic win for us.\" Japan levelled the score twice, through Ben Gunter and Warner Dearns, and Shinya Komura's try four minutes from time left Wales holding on by a single score. Jones said his young side stuck at it but did not take points from its time in Wales's 22, which he said is the way the game now works."
        },
