    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Murrayfield win",
          "heading": "All Blacks beat Scotland 43-21 at Murrayfield despite Ewan Ashman's first-half hat-trick",
          "body": "Scotland could not score in the second half, and New Zealand ran in seven tries to three at Murrayfield on Saturday. Hooker Ewan Ashman scored a first-half hat-trick, but the All Blacks led 24-21 at the break and their second-half surge settled it, with Josh Moorby, Beauden Barrett and Asafo Aumua scoring after the interval. Wallace Sititi and Peter Lakai both visited the sin bin in the first half. Scotland coach Gregor Townsend said: \"And it wasn't there today. So that's frustrating.\""
        },
        {
